.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
CPP-API: Primary logging facility of \fBAssimp\fP\&. 

The library stores its primary \fBLogger\fP as a static member of this class\&. \fBget()\fP returns this primary logger\&. By default the underlying implementation is just a #NullLogger which rejects all log messages\&. By calling \fBcreate()\fP, logging is turned on\&. To capture the log output multiple log streams (#LogStream) can be attach to the logger\&. Some default streams for common streaming locations (such as a file, std::cout, OutputDebugString()) are also provided\&.
.PP
If you wish to customize the logging at an even deeper level supply your own implementation of \fBLogger\fP to \fBset()\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The whole logging stuff causes a small extra overhead for all imports\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "bool Assimp::DefaultLogger::attachStream (\fBLogStream\fP * pStream, unsigned int severity)\fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Attach a new log-stream\&.    The logger takes ownership of the stream and is responsible for its destruction (which is done using delete when the logger itself is destroyed)\&. Call detachStream to detach a stream and to gain ownership of it again\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpStream\fP Log-stream to attach 
.br
\fIseverity\fP Message filter, specified which types of log messages are dispatched to the stream\&. Provide a bitwise combination of the ErrorSeverity flags\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the stream has been attached, false otherwise\&.    
.br
 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implements \fBAssimp::Logger\fP\&.
.SS "static \fBLogger\fP * Assimp::DefaultLogger::create (const char * name = \fR\fBASSIMP_DEFAULT_LOG_NAME\fP\fP, \fBLogSeverity\fP severity = \fR\fBNORMAL\fP\fP, unsigned int defStreams = \fR\fBaiDefaultLogStream_DEBUGGER\fP|\fBaiDefaultLogStream_FILE\fP\fP, \fBIOSystem\fP * io = \fRnullptr\fP)\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Creates a logging instance\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP Name for log file\&. Only valid in combination with the aiDefaultLogStream_FILE flag\&. 
.br
\fIseverity\fP Log severity, DEBUG turns on debug messages and VERBOSE turns on all messages\&. 
.br
\fIdefStreams\fP Default log streams to be attached\&. Any bitwise combination of the aiDefaultLogStream enumerated values\&. If \fBaiDefaultLogStream_FILE\fP is specified but an empty string is passed for 'name', no log file is created at all\&. 
.br
\fIio\fP \fBIOSystem\fP to be used to open external files (such as the log file)\&. Pass nullptr to rely on the default implementation\&. This replaces the default #NullLogger with a DefaultLogger instance\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "bool Assimp::DefaultLogger::detachStream (\fBLogStream\fP * pStream, unsigned int severity)\fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Detach a still attached stream from the logger (or modify the filter flags bits)    
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpStream\fP Log-stream instance for detaching 
.br
\fIseverity\fP Provide a bitwise combination of the ErrorSeverity flags\&. This value is &~ed with the current flags of the stream, if the result is 0 the stream is detached from the \fBLogger\fP and the caller retakes the possession of the stream\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the stream has been detached, false otherwise\&.    
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implements \fBAssimp::Logger\fP\&.
